course: dictionary
lesson: 15570
title: One word, four meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can find the right one by reading the words around it. The word «suspended» can mean hung from above, stopped for a time, sent away from school or play as a punishment, or floating in a liquid.
explain: «The lamp was suspended from the ceiling.» The clues are lamp and ceiling, so suspended means hung from above. «The football match was suspended because of heavy rain.» The clue is rain, so suspended means stopped for a time, not for ever.
explain: Suspended is also the past form of the verb suspend, so you may also see suspend, suspends and suspending. Always test your meaning: put it in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Suspended can mean hung from above, stopped for a time, or floating in a liquid.
fact: «The pupil was suspended for fighting.» Here suspended means not allowed to come to school for a time, as a punishment.
fact: «Tiny grains of sand were suspended in the water.» Here suspended means floating in the water without sinking or rising.
fact: The verb suspend has the forms suspend, suspends, suspended and suspending.
fact: Clue words such as ceiling, rain or fighting show you which meaning is right.
exercise: «The lamp was suspended from the ceiling.» What does suspended mean here? | Sent home as a punishment | *Hung from above | Floating in water | Stopped for a time
exercise: «The school match was suspended because of the storm.» What does suspended mean here? | *Stopped for a time, not for ever | Given a prize | Made into a loud noise | Hung from a rope
exercise: «Sand was suspended in the glass of water.» What does suspended mean here? | Dropped to the bottom | Boiled away | *Floating without sinking or rising | Frozen solid
test: «Ella was suspended from school for one day.» What does suspended mean here? | Stopped for ever | *Not allowed to come to school for a time, as a punishment | Hung from above | Floating in a liquid
test: Which word is a form of the verb suspend? | suspect | suspicious | suspense | *suspending
exam: «The bridge was suspended over the river.» What does suspended mean here? | Floating in the river | Sent away as a punishment | Stopped for a time | *Hung up high above
